<Layout
  title="Document Encryption Standards | usignpdf"
  seo={{
    page_description: "Understand how usignpdf protects your sensitive contracts with AES-256 encryption at rest and TLS in transit.",
    canonical_url: "https://usignpdf.com/security/encryption/"
  }}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-20 px-4 md:px-8 prose">
    <a href="/security" class="text-accent no-underline hover:underline">&larr; Back to Security</a>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mt-8 mb-8">Encryption & Data Protection</h1>

    <p>Your contracts contain sensitive business information. We treat them accordingly.</p>

    <h2>Encryption in Transit</h2>
    <p>All data sent between your browser, your clients' browsers, and our servers is encrypted using <strong>TLS 1.3</strong> (Transport Layer Security). This prevents man-in-the-middle attacks and ensures data privacy during transfer.</p>

    <h2>Encryption at Rest</h2>
    <p>When your documents are stored on our servers waiting to be signed, they are encrypted using <strong>AES-256</strong> (Advanced Encryption Standard). This is the same encryption standard used by banks and the US government for top-secret information.</p>

    <h2>Document Deletion</h2>
    <p>We are not a permanent file storage service. We recommend downloading your completed PDFs. You can request immediate deletion of your documents from our servers at any time.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
